Bond yields have been the only story on anyone's timeline for three days.

Inside Real Vision two key pieces landed in forty-eight hours.

@AndreasSteno  Tuesday morning, before the panic peaked: a higher long end is what the system needs right now, as long as it arrives through a steeper curve. His bottom line is to stop fearing the long end and start fearing a flat curve.

@RaoulGMI Wednesday, after the US Treasury doubled its buybacks: For the first time the fiscal authority, not the Fed, stepped in to defend the long end within a day of the highs. His bottom line is that there is now a ceiling on the long bond and the market has just been told where it is.

Two reads, forty-eight hours apart, on the thing everyone else was just shouting about.

